{"availability":"available","full":"jkspeaks/deterministic-trader","name":"deterministic-trader","description":"An AI trading agent that is never allowed to make a trading decision. Deterministic Python core. Every rule is in tested code, not prompt text.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-12T03:20:15Z","updated":"2026-10-12T03:45:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["agentic-trading","ai-trading-system","algorithmic-trading","claude","mcp","robinhood","robinhood-api","supabase","telegrambot","trading-bot","vercel"],"demo":"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.626Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.626Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.626Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.626Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An AI agent that trades a real brokerage account, and is never allowed to make a trading decision.","A complete, unattended swing-trading system for one cash brokerage account. A deterministic Python core holds every rule: what to buy, how much, when to sell, and every reason to refuse. A scheduled Claude session is only the hands. It fetches broker data, hands it to the core, and places exactly the orders the plan names, at the prices the plan gives.","The result is an agent you can audit. Every decision is a pure function of stored inputs, so it can be replayed offline, tested, and measured against a rule change before that change touches money."],"features":["The whole system, not a demo. Strategies, sizing, risk guard, broker reconciliation, a database schema, scheduled jobs, alerting, operator controls, a backtest engine and the prompts the agent runs. Nothing is left as…","The model cannot improvise a trade. It places only what plan.orders, plan.protection and plan.cancels name. The plan is written to the run log before anything is placed.","Decisions are reproducible. The core has no network access, and a test proves it. Stored cycle inputs are replayed nightly against rule variants, so a rule change is measured before it trades.","It fails closed. Missing data, an ambiguous broker answer, a stale universe or an implausible account read each stop new entries. Exits are still placed.","It checks its own book. Every reconciling cycle compares the broker's positions and orders with what the system intended and classifies each disagreement. It never silently repairs one."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkspeaks/deterministic-trader/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d00c14b00be343af9a1f67beb039babbe3e546d78766394182b2844924851aca","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.759Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.759Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An AI agent that trades a real brokerage account, and is never allowed to make a trading decision.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkspeaks/deterministic-trader/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No accounts, no API keys, no network.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkspeaks/deterministic-trader/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Fixed titles for the events that matter: Drawdown halt, Account read implausible, Order refused, Manual action required, Cycle stalled, Cycle over budget, Weekly scorecard, and more.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkspeaks/deterministic-trader/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"d00c14b00be343af9a1f67beb039babbe3e546d78766394182b2844924851aca","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkspeaks/deterministic-trader/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.760Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-12T03:45:15Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jkspeaks/deterministic-trader/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:34.764Z","hash":"d00c14b00be343af9